<title>TURKEY: Turk Otosan 9-mth profits jump 378 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Otosan 9-mth profits jump 378 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	4,547.38  vs     950.81</p>
<p>    Net profit			 6,002.54  vs   1,255.07</p>
<p>    Net sales			 26,412.88  vs   9,920.43</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 7,385.45  vs   1,823.60</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     1,999.59  vs     217.09</p>
<p>    Interest paid			  7.57  vs	 2.98</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense		132.39  vs     101.44</p>
<p>    Total debts			8,180.12  vs   2,699.80</p>
<p>    Equity			    10,587.66  vs   3,775.38</p>
<p>    Capital			    1,320.00  vs   1,320.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Commercial vehicle and passenger car producer Otosan Otomobil Sanayii A.S. is owned 30 percent by Ford Motor Co and 53.9 percent by Turkey's leading industrial Koc group and Koc family.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875 EKS</p>
</text>
